Surfaced while fixing karr #87.

api_key_env (Langertha::Engine::Remote:42, karr #44) is documented as "the environment
variable this engine reads its API key from ... Returns undef for engines that do not
require an API key". That is a two-state answer for a three-state world:

  required   -> LANGERTHA_<VENDOR>_API_KEY   (cloud engines)
  optional   -> reads an env var, works without it
  none       -> undef

The optional case now exists twice and both engines answer undef while quietly reading an
env var:

  Engine::LMStudio / LMStudioOpenAI / LMStudioAnthropic -> LANGERTHA_LMSTUDIO_API_KEY
  Engine::Ollama / OllamaOpenAI (karr #87)              -> LANGERTHA_OLLAMA_API_KEY

#87 followed the LMStudio precedent (undef) rather than inventing a third convention
mid-fix, and t/10_engine_hierarchy.t:838ff pins Ollama/OllamaOpenAI/LMStudio* into the
"keyless -> undef" list.

Consequence for the consumer that motivated #44: Langertha::Knarr scanning the environment
for configurable engines will not discover that LANGERTHA_OLLAMA_API_KEY unlocks Ollama
Cloud, or that LANGERTHA_LMSTUDIO_API_KEY unlocks a secured LM Studio.

Options: (a) leave as is and document "optional keys are not advertised"; (b) have
api_key_env name the var it actually reads and add a separate api_key_required predicate;
(c) return a small structure. Whichever wins, do it for LMStudio and Ollama in one move —
the two must not diverge.
Option (b) implemented: api_key_env now names the variable the engine actually reads; a new
class method api_key_required (Engine::Remote) carries the mandatory/optional bit.

Why (b) over (a)/(c):
- (a) documents the gap away, but the gap IS the feature #44 asked for -- a consumer scanning
  the environment must be able to see that LANGERTHA_OLLAMA_API_KEY unlocks Ollama Cloud.
  "We do not advertise optional keys" would force Knarr to keep the hand-maintained table
  that #44 exists to delete.
- (c) (hashref) answers the same two questions but forces every consumer to destructure and
  breaks the shape of the neighbouring introspection methods (default_model, tool_wire_format
  -- plain scalar class methods).
- (b) keeps the scalar ergonomics, adds one orthogonal predicate, and each of the three states
  stays independently assertable.

Cost of the break: none externally. api_key_env landed in 43e5603, after the 0.502 tag, and is
in no released version (`git tag --contains 43e5603` is empty). Nothing in lib/ consumes it
(only engine definitions + tests); Langertha::Knarr still scans with its own @ENGINE_DEFS and
so far only consumes default_model_for.

Default in Engine::Remote: api_key_required { defined $class->api_key_env ? 1 : 0 }. Cloud
engines and no-env engines therefore need no override at all -- only the optional group opts
out, which is exactly the group that is special.

Engines pulled along (all five that read an env var while answering undef):
  Ollama            override dropped (derivation already yields LANGERTHA_OLLAMA_API_KEY) + required 0
  OllamaOpenAI      api_key_env 'LANGERTHA_OLLAMA_API_KEY' (derivation would say OLLAMAOPENAI) + required 0
  LMStudio          override dropped (derivation correct) + required 0
  LMStudioOpenAI    api_key_env 'LANGERTHA_LMSTUDIO_API_KEY' + required 0
  LMStudioAnthropic api_key_env 'LANGERTHA_LMSTUDIO_API_KEY' + required 0
Convention followed: override api_key_env only where derivation is wrong, as the cloud engines do.

NOT pulled along: vLLM, SGLang, LlamaCpp, Whisper read no env var at all, so undef stays the
honest answer and required derives to 0. Giving them an optional env key is a behaviour change,
not a semantics fix -- filed separately.

Tests: t/10_engine_hierarchy.t part 6b restructured into the three states (required / optional /
none) and it now also pins that the advertised name is the name actually read (set
$ENV{advertised} -> the built api_key carries it). t/13_ollama_auth.t tail updated. Suite:
prove -lr t/ = 86 files / 2724 tests, all green, offline (every *API_KEY* var unset for the run,
live tests skipped). perlcritic --profile .perlcriticrc lib/ bin/ maint/ clean. Not committed,
not staged.

Stale but harmless: docs/adr/0016 line 110 quotes "Engine::Ollama has sub api_key_env { undef }
